Polars allows you to insert a column into a dataframe at any position you want. Below is a dataframe showing the ratings of some unknown movies.

**ratings_df**

::: {#6ca432b9 .cell execution_count=1}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (4, 3)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>year</th><th>rating</th><th>minutes</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>f64</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2011</td><td>7.1</td><td>107</td></tr><tr><td>1999</td><td>6.4</td><td>101</td></tr><tr><td>2000</td><td>7.0</td><td>120</td></tr><tr><td>2017</td><td>6.8</td><td>133</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


**movie_title_column**

::: {#7c26a618 .cell execution_count=2}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (4,)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>movie</th></tr><tr><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Margin Call&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Rogue Trader&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Boiler Room&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;The Wizard of Lies&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


## Insert column into dataframe

To insert another column into the dataframe above, make sure the column type is `series`, not `dataframe`. Here’s how you can insert a new column as the first column in the dataframe:

::: {#7530ddd6 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(ratings_df
 .insert_column(0, movie_title_column)
 )
```

